{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For yet seven days.</b> Besides the fact that they had a period of 120 years to repent, I am further granting them an extension of seven days. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: these are the seven days of mourning for Methuselah the righteous, for which the Holy One, blessed be He, held back His world and did not bring the Flood, in his honor. And this is what it says immediately afterward: ״ויהי לשבעת הימים ומי המבול היו על הארץ״ — 'And it came to pass after the seven days, and the waters of the Flood were upon the earth.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:55.495527984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}